body:
Good job overall! Your output should be correct, as you followed the instructions exactly.

Another small thing that, while not an error by any means, is interesting to note: you don't need to provide a formal parameter like `e` to these `catch` statements. If you don't use the thrown exception in your catch behavior, you can simply omit the formal and have statements like this:

```c++
catch (char) { cout << "G-" << endl; }
catch (double) { cout << "H-" << endl; }
```

